# Graph Health & Self-Test

Spec: GraphHealth
Purpose:
  Define the self-test mechanism for the .sdd system. The graph
  must be able to validate itself for consistency, completeness,
  and drift.

Owns: graph/health.sdd

HealthMetrics:
  Knowledge:
    concepts: 183
    active: 161
    dormant: 12
    deprecated: 10
    broken_references: 2
    unverified: 7

  Graph:
    isolated_nodes
    orphan_tasks
    broken_edges
    duplicate_concepts
    conflicting_decisions
    stale_references
    circular_dependencies

SelfTest:
  questions the system auto-asks:
    - Are all active skills referenced?
    - Are all critical decisions evidenced?
    - Are all tasks connected to a goal?
    - Are all architecture rules applicable?
    - Are deprecated references still used?
    - Are there contradictory decisions?

SDDSelfReview:
  evolution: CODE → REVIEW becomes SDD → SELF REVIEW
  check:
    - drift between .sdd and source code
    - architecture drift (decision says DDD, code shows anemic model)
    - principle violations (SOLID, KISS, YAGNI, DRY, CLEAR_ARCH)
    - stale knowledge (unused concepts, orphaned tasks)

DeadKnowledge:
  detection: @skill.old-payment
    references: 0
    used_by: 0
  classification:
    ACTIVE     — in use
    DORMANT    — unused but potentially valid
    DEPRECATED — superseded by newer knowledge
    ARCHIVED   — historical, no longer relevant
  rule: dead knowledge is flagged, not immediately deleted

ArchitectureDrift:
  detection:
    Decision: @decision.D88 architecture: DDD
    Code: controller → repository → database (no domain layer)
  system: ARCHITECTURE_DRIFT
  resolution: @skill.evolution-review

ViolationDetection:
  @violation.V22
  principle: KISS
  found_in: payment/service.go
  reason: unnecessary abstraction
  resolution: removed abstraction

  flow:
    CODE → REVIEW → VIOLATION → PATTERN → KNOWLEDGE → SKILL → PREVENTION

State: +
